 of Doubting Thomas, Mary Magdalene, and Judas Iscariot in Early Christian Literature","full_title":"Gospels of the Marginalized The Redemption of Doubting Thomas, Mary Magdalene, and Judas Iscariot in Early Christian Literature","works":[{"key":"/works/OL20547950W"}],"key":"/books/OL34049648M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-09-29T21:53:08.286792"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-09-29T21:53:08.286792"}}},"ISBN:9781620322680":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781620322680","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27791061M/The_Gospels_of_the_marginalized","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/gospelsofmargina0000meye","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10014696-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Cascade Books"],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Introduction","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Thomas","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Mary Magdalene","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Judas Iscariot","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Epilogue : Gospel of the Redeemed : draft chapters in a gospel of wisdom, with restored disciples.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The Gospels of the Marginalized provides an exciting new study of three of the most maligned figures in the New Testament story of Jesus: Thomas, usually considered the quintessential doubter among the disciples; Mary Magdalene, characterized as a repentant prostitute during much of the history of the church; and Judas Iscariot, presented as the despicable disciple of Jesus who betrayed his master for money. In this book Marvin Meyer, one of the most prominent of the scholars of gnostic texts and other early Christian literature, offers fresh and accurate translations of the Gospels of Thomas, Mary, and Judas, with their proclamation of the good news of the wisdom of Jesus, and he uses these gospels as the occasion to reexamine the place of Thomas, Mary Magdalene, and Judas Iscariot in the Jesus movement. His striking analysis suggests that Thomas was no doubter, that Mary Magdalene was a beloved disciple in the inner circles of disciples around Jesus, and that the tale of Judas Iscariot as betrayer of Jesus is a piece of fiction. Meyer adds a Gospel of the Redeemed as a vivid illustration of how the gospel story of Jesus might read with Jesus as a Jewish teacher of wisdom and Thomas, Mary, and Judas restored as loyal followers of the teacher from Nazareth."},"isbn_10":["1620322684"],"covers":[10014696],"lc_classifications":["BT1390 .M49 2012"],"key":"/books/OL27791061M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1400672A","name":"Marvin W. Meyer"}],"ocaid":"gospelsofmargina0000meye","publish_places":["Eugene, Or"],"subjects":["Gospel of Judas","Gospel of Mary","Literatur","Evangelium Mariae","Criticism, interpretation","History and criticism","Gospel of Thomas (Coptic Gospel)","Sources","Early Christian literature","Evangelium Thomae","Gnosticism","Evangelium des Judas","Frühchristentum"],"isbn_13":["9781620322680"],"pagination":"x, 156 pages","source_records":["marc:marc_marygrove/marygrovecollegelibrary.full.D20191108.T213022.internetarchive2nd_REPACK.mrc:195715091:4088","ia:gospelsofmargina0000meye","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part40.utf8:146679157:1328","bwb:9781620322680","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-021.mrc:82037516:1159","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:771822017:1460"],"subtitle":"the redemption of Doubting Thomas, Mary Magdalene, and Judas Iscariot in early Christian literature","title":"The Gospels of the marginalized","lccn":["2012532340"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (pages 129-143) and index.\n\nInternet Archive - 2\n\nIntern